  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women&apos;s Empowerment in Credit &amp; Savings</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Members of the village savings and loans associations meet regularly to put money into their association&apos;s savings and to loan their growing funds to members. In contrast to microfinance institutions, the interest paid on credit goes back into the communal pot so members see their savings increase over time.The Artisanal Mining Women&apos;s Empowerment Credit &amp; Savings project (AFECCOR) facilitates sensitisation on gender equality and lead discussions with female members of associations and their partners about household finances to challenge traditional stereotypes and gender roles. AFECCOR provides financial literacy training to women who access credit from their association to undertake new entrepreneurial activities around mine sites.For more information about this project, please visit the project overview on the EPRM website.</narrative>
  </description>
